WEBVTT

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:17.250
Ah! I slept really well.

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:20.140
I wonder how many months it's been
since I was able to relax like this.

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:25.700
What bliss to be able to stay in Avonlea
for three months before going to Redmond.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:31.070
I feel so contented.

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:55.960
Ah! I finally feel like I've come home.

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:10.050
Anne! Anne! It's time for breakfast!

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.550
Oh dear! Is it that late already?

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:17.120
Good morning.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:18.650
I'm sorry I overslept.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:21.990
You've come home after a
long absence. It's no wonder.

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:24.050
- Now, sit down.
- Yes.

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:25.060
Good morning, Matthew.

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:28.990
Good morning. It's good that you
took your time to sleep.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:32.850
I kept saying that we shouldn't wake you up yet.

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:34.730
What are you saying?

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:38.610
Matthew has been waiting a long
time to have breakfast with you.

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:42.330
No... Well, since your holiday is long...

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:44.640
Thank you, Matthew.

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:49.420
Oh yes. This is Martin. He came to help us last month.

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:51.680
Anne-san, I went ahead and ate.

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.250
I have to sow the turnips.

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:55.420
I'm sorry for being late.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:56.720
It's all right.

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:04.300
Well, I'll take my leave now.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.170
Yes. Thank you.

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:12.420
Martin is a hard worker.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:15.430
He has a lot of experience,
and he's helped us a lot.

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:18.460
I see. That's good, Matthew.

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:20.720
Yes, thank goodness.

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:25.380
Matthew doesn't work too much anymore,
and so, I feel relieved.

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:26.710
Well, shall we eat?

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.570
Yes. Let's eat.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:44.320
Thank you for the food!
Ah, I'm so full.

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:46.380
It's been a long time
since I had your hot biscuits.

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.700
They're so delicious
that I ate too many.

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:50.760
Oh, I see.

00:04:58.180 --> 00:04:59.610
I'm going out now.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:01.700
You mustn't overwork yourself!

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:03.130
Yes, I know.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.040
Take care!

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:06.040
Yes.

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:14.790
Marilla, how is Matthew?

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.880
He doesn't look too good.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:20.330
That's true. Maybe he's just getting old.

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:22.040
Anne, listen.

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:24.860
Since you came home on that snowy day,

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:32.130
he's had a few severe attacks.
And he refuses to rest.

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:35.090
I'm also very worried.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:39.120
But he hasn't had any seizures lately,

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.120
and since we've found a good worker,

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:45.110
I think he might recuperate and get better.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:49.960
But now that you're home,
Anne, I'm sure he will.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:53.930
Whenever you are here,
he seems to become better.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.590
But it seems like you're not as
healthy as you used to be either.

00:05:58.780 --> 00:05:59.980
You seem to be very tired.

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:03.020
Do I look tired?

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:05.440
It's just my age catching up with me.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:09.280
And it's not because I have too much work.

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:10.780
It's because of my head.

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:15.650
I get headaches very often,
and my eyes hurt, too.

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:23.220
Dr. Spencer has examined me,
but he is unable to find the cause.

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:27.230
I heard that an eye specialist

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:29.430
will come to this island at
the end of this month.

00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:33.450
Dr. Spencer suggested consulting him,
and I thought I would do that.

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:37.940
Yes. You should let him examine you.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:42.120
It's so troublesome to
read and sew these days.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:48.380
Marilla, now that I am home,
you should rest.

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:52.880
If I can take this one
day to visit an old friend,

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:55.090
I will help you around
the house from tomorrow on.

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:56.900
I want you to take it easy, Marilla.

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:06.860
Anyway, you really did well.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:12.210
You got a First Class certificate in one year,
and you were able to get a scholarship.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:15.490
That was excellent. I'm so proud of you.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:19.160
Rachel always says "Pride goes before a fall",

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:23.420
and that it's no good thing for a
woman to get higher education.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:25.820
I don't agree at all.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:30.780
Marilla! I'm glad to hear you say that.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:37.990
Anyway, since you will be going to University,
you can use the money you got from the school,

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:41.600
and it's not like we don't
have some savings as well.

00:07:42.470 --> 00:07:46.270
Since we can leave the
main work to Martin now,

00:07:46.310 --> 00:07:50.410
there's less to worry about.

00:07:51.850 --> 00:07:53.840
Well, thinking about worries...

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:57.450
Good morning, Marilla!

00:07:57.650 --> 00:07:59.140
Oh, Rachel. Good morning.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:01.820
What are you doing here
so early in the morning?

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:03.450
Good morning, Mrs. Lynde.

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:05.290
Oh, Anne. Welcome home.

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:07.130
Marilla, is Matthew home?

00:08:07.160 --> 00:08:10.260
Yes. But he just left for the field.
Is there some urgent business?

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:11.160
Yes.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:18.100
It seems like the rumors are true.
Abbey Bank is on the verge of collapse.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:19.430
Hold on, Mrs. Lynde.

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:21.410
Anne, go get Matthew.

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:22.680
Yes.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:24.910
Don't mention anything
to him just yet!

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:26.380
I understand, Marilla.

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:42.640
Brother, please listen calmly
to what I have to say.

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:47.860
We have to get our money out
of Abbey Bank very quickly.

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:52.190
Matthew Cuthbert, my husband heard
the rumor in town.

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:55.460
It will happen within the next few weeks.

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:59.120
They were unable to collect a large amount of their loans.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:01.790
I told you that it was a reliable fact.

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:04.940
People rushed in great numbers
to the bank yesterday.

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:10.210
Please remain calm. The bankruptcy of
Abbey Bank was only a matter of time.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:11.620
Bankruptcy...

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:15.230
It would be terrible if it was true.

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:19.600
I heard that Abbey Bank is your only bank.

00:09:22.140 --> 00:09:23.270
What do you think, Brother?

00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:29.570
I think we should listen to Rachel's advice
and take out our money from the bank.

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:32.810
N-No... Well, now...

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:34.790
But the other day, at Blair's,

00:09:34.820 --> 00:09:39.050
I heard it's just a groundless rumor started by
people who are against the bank.

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:42.490
And Mr. Abbey and I...

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:45.410
I know he was a close friend to your father,

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:48.500
and I understand you want to believe in Mr. Abbey.

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:50.590
But the real power of the bank

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:52.680
seems to have already fallen
into the hands of his nephew.

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:56.840
Moreover, it has been said that their
new financial plan has failed.

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:02.510
Anne, did you hear anything about it
while you were in town?

00:10:02.550 --> 00:10:07.550
I think Miss Barry brought it up,
but I'm not sure.

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:14.150
Matthew, even if you don't trust me,
shouldn't you go and see for yourself?

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:16.420
Meet someone with reliable information.

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:18.790
If the need arises, I can go with you.

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:22.460
That's right. Matthew, what do you think about that?

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:25.490
Rachel came all the way here with the news.

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:27.330
Well, now...

00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:32.930
I don't think there's cause for worry.

00:10:32.980 --> 00:10:38.000
Well then, I'll go to meet Mr. Russel
and hear what he has to say.

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:40.870
I think he should know about this.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:47.580
Matthew, you must take the money out
if things don't go well.

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:50.320
It's not the time for loyalty now.

00:10:50.360 --> 00:10:51.590
You're right about that.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:53.560
Yes. I understand that.

00:11:26.460 --> 00:11:31.590
Oh, Matthew Cuthbert.
It's been a long time.

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:34.230
So, what do you want to talk about?

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:38.880
Well, that....
Actually, it's about Abbey Bank.

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:40.290
Ah!

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:44.960
How surprising! I didn't think
you'd be worried by such rumors.

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:47.690
No, I...

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:51.250
Now, now. Please come this way.

00:11:54.690 --> 00:11:57.220
N-No, I...

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:03.930
Well, Matthew Cuthbert,
I'm telling you frankly,

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:06.460
although this was not made public,

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:11.530
Abbey Bank was going through
a crisis a while ago,

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:13.410
but everything's all right now.

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:15.280
At present, we mean to reconstruct,

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:20.210
and all major banks have
promised me complete support.

00:12:20.600 --> 00:12:24.810
Mr. Russel, are you sure about that?

00:12:24.860 --> 00:12:29.140
I'm one of the major creditors
of the bank. I wouldn't lie.

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:34.400
Oh, I see. I'm relieved.

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:40.230
I'm not worried in the least,
but everyone else...

00:12:40.270 --> 00:12:43.160
...thinks that the bank is going bankrupt tomorrow?

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:46.130
Well, now. That's what they say.

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:51.120
Matthew Cuthbert, those are
merely unfounded rumors.

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:54.810
Some people have conspired against Mr. Abbey,

00:12:54.820 --> 00:12:58.050
in order to make people
withdraw their deposits.

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:03.120
Because of their scheming, I cannot
assert that it is 100% all right anymore.

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:07.150
If old business partners like us

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:13.080
don't panic and are swayed by such rumors,
Abbey Bank will stand fast.

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:15.930
Savings is the lifeline of any bank.

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:21.240
I didn't intend to take my money out.

00:13:21.460 --> 00:13:22.710
Of course you don't.

00:13:24.180 --> 00:13:27.780
I heard about the girl you took charge of.

00:13:28.150 --> 00:13:32.050
I heard she's a genius and that she
has gotten a place at Redmond College.

00:13:32.090 --> 00:13:34.390
You must be very proud of her.

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:38.790
Yes, of course, as you were saying...

00:13:41.330 --> 00:13:46.460
She's not only intelligent, she's a dear.

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:50.600
You seem to dote on her. That's great.

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:55.200
I hope you will continue to support Abbey Bank.

00:13:55.250 --> 00:14:00.810
Well, now... I was never worried about it.

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:04.710
Well, I'm really glad I came here today.

00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:07.950
It was good of you to come, Mr. Cuthbert.

00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:24.100
I see.

00:14:24.680 --> 00:14:28.960
But one can never be sure when something
like this will happen to a bank.

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:34.540
Didn't you mention taking
half of our savings out?

00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:37.080
Don't worry, Marilla.

00:14:37.240 --> 00:14:41.610
Mr. Russel seemed very calm.
There's no mistake.

00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:46.240
Also, I believe in Mr. Abbey.

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:50.190
Well, if you really think so.

00:14:50.900 --> 00:14:52.780
Let's just wait for a while.

00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:56.520
It will be all right, Marilla.

00:14:57.210 --> 00:14:58.800
I'm leaving now.

00:14:58.950 --> 00:15:01.260
Yes. Don't overwork yourself.

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:02.830
I know that.

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:04.520
- Take care!
- Yes.

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:08.970
Is this really all right, Marilla?

00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:11.530
Yes. It should be.

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:14.440
Matthew's intuition has always
been pretty accurate.

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:19.100
Maybe it's just like Matthew said,
and the reconstruction has already started.

00:15:19.150 --> 00:15:21.480
It's all right. There's nothing to worry about.

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:25.960
Yes. Everything will be fine.

00:15:26.640 --> 00:15:31.090
When you've finished washing up,
you want to outside today, don't you?

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:33.680
The forest and the spring you named are waiting for you.

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:36.130
Oh yes! I nearly forgot that.

00:15:36.210 --> 00:15:39.220
Please let me be selfish and
have this one day for myself, Marilla.

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:42.100
It's all right. It's your long awaited holiday.

00:17:06.620 --> 00:17:08.520
That is so great.

00:17:09.010 --> 00:17:11.780
When I and my husband heard
that you got the Avery scholarship,

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:15.610
we couldn't help calling out
'Congratulations, Anne Shirley!'

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:20.120
And of course we gave
thanks to the Lord as well.

00:17:20.170 --> 00:17:23.160
Thank you, Mrs. Alan.

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:25.630
You are at your peak now.

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:27.690
Now that you've decided to enter university,

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:31.600
you can spend time happily
dreaming about the future.

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:35.710
Matthew and Marilla must be delighted.

00:17:35.850 --> 00:17:39.230
Yes, they are very happy for me.

00:17:40.360 --> 00:17:41.090
But...

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:42.790
But what?

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:48.820
I realize now that both Matthew
and Marilla have aged a lot.

00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:53.270
I have to leave them for another
four years to be at Redmond.

00:17:53.930 --> 00:17:54.830
Somehow, I...

00:17:58.170 --> 00:18:02.840
I feel as if I should stay here
and them help out in the house.

00:18:04.110 --> 00:18:08.310
I see. So that's how it is.

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:10.990
It's only natural that you are troubled.

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:14.580
They are both getting on in age.

00:18:17.390 --> 00:18:22.390
So have you given up on university
and decided to stay here?

00:18:22.690 --> 00:18:23.460
What?

00:18:24.030 --> 00:18:26.640
No, I haven't made up my mind yet.

00:18:27.300 --> 00:18:31.170
That's true. You worry about them,

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:35.140
yet you do not want to
give up your bright future.

00:18:35.180 --> 00:18:40.340
In fact, you want to go your
own way even more, don't you?

00:18:40.380 --> 00:18:43.660
Yes. That's why this is so painful.

00:18:44.250 --> 00:18:48.480
Then, though it's painful, you have no
choice but to go to Redmond College.

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:53.120
If you give up going to university,
and become a teacher here,

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:57.200
Matthew and Marilla will probably be very glad.

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:59.150
That would be easy to do, wouldn't it?

00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:02.520
But if you give up on your dreams,

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:05.360
don't you think you will regret
it for the rest of your life?

00:19:05.680 --> 00:19:06.320
Yes.

00:19:06.640 --> 00:19:07.660
But...

00:19:07.710 --> 00:19:13.610
No, Anne. Even though it's painful,
we humans cannot avoid worries.

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:16.110
It is what's called conscience.

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:23.320
If they are happy that you got
a place in the university,

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:25.590
you should remember this.

00:19:25.630 --> 00:19:29.200
Bring your troubles with you and
graduate from university with the best results.

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:31.150
That is the road you should take.

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:34.530
Also, isn't that what the two of them expect?

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:39.940
I'm glad that you think about these things.

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:44.740
If you had become arrogant about
getting a place at university,

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:46.150
you would have been a failure.

00:19:49.420 --> 00:19:52.380
There's no need to make
sense of everything, Anne.

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:55.710
No... Don't think you can
make sense of everything.

00:19:57.860 --> 00:20:04.290
Although I can't be sure that your
problems can be solved here,

00:20:04.330 --> 00:20:06.420
do you understand what I am saying?

00:20:06.450 --> 00:20:07.990
Yes, Mrs. Alan.

00:20:08.360 --> 00:20:15.030
Although I'm still troubled,
I'll think about what you said.

00:20:15.070 --> 00:20:17.470
Have some cake.

00:20:17.510 --> 00:20:19.230
I will. Thank you.

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:39.590
Matthew! Matthew!

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:50.390
Welcome back, Anne.

00:20:50.740 --> 00:20:52.590
I'm back, Matthew.

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:56.000
- That is your Dolly.
- Oh my!

00:20:56.930 --> 00:21:01.670
She's at her most mischievous now.
She wanders away all the time.

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:04.630
Cows grow amazingly fast, don't they?

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:08.900
Yes, Anne. Just like you.

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:10.040
Really?

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:17.250
Today, I visited a lot of
places with old memories.

00:21:17.290 --> 00:21:20.010
Starting tomorrow, I'm going
to work hard to help you.

00:21:20.390 --> 00:21:26.350
Well, now, Anne. This is your long awaited
holiday, so you should take it easy.

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:29.910
You and Marilla deserve
a rest more than I do.

00:21:30.930 --> 00:21:36.660
You are working too hard again.
Why can't you take things easy?

00:21:36.710 --> 00:21:41.580
Well, now. I can't seem to do that.

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:47.030
I always forget that I'm getting older.

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:52.750
Well, since I have been
working very hard up until now,

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:55.380
I want to keep doing that until I die.

00:22:01.100 --> 00:22:04.310
If only I had been the boy
you had sent for,

00:22:04.770 --> 00:22:06.880
I would be able to help you out.

00:22:07.120 --> 00:22:09.930
In many ways, I was raised in comfort.

00:22:10.210 --> 00:22:15.470
When I think that,
I really wish I were a boy.

00:22:15.600 --> 00:22:16.830
Well, now.

00:22:17.960 --> 00:22:19.680
But Anne,

00:22:19.720 --> 00:22:25.090
I'd rather have you than a dozen boys.

00:22:27.320 --> 00:22:31.760
Listen, I would never exchange
you for a dozen of them.

00:22:31.920 --> 00:22:33.590
Well, now.

00:22:33.780 --> 00:22:38.460
The one who got the Avery scholarship
wasn't a boy, mind you,

00:22:38.500 --> 00:22:40.330
but a girl.

00:22:40.370 --> 00:22:46.570
You're my girl. My my very own girl.

00:22:46.860 --> 00:22:47.830
Matthew...

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:51.640
Anne, you are my daughter.

00:23:00.920 --> 00:23:01.620
Matthew.

00:23:38.560 --> 00:23:43.590
The peaceful beauty and the fragrant scent of this night

00:23:43.630 --> 00:23:46.260
will become a very important part
of Anne's memories.

00:23:47.170 --> 00:23:54.080
That's because it is the last night
before sorrow touches her life.

00:24:05.460 --> 00:24:08.340
Next on Anne of Green Gables:
Episode 47

00:24:08.770 --> 00:24:10.660
The Reaper Whose Name Is Death

00:24:10.700 --> 00:24:11.800
Please look forward to it!

00:24:12.100 --> 00:24:16.420
The Adventures of Tom Sawyer

00:24:16.420 --> 00:24:18.680
Taking place in the grand nature surrounding Mississippi,

00:24:18.680 --> 00:24:22.170
Tom Sawyer and his friends
experience pleasant adventures.

00:24:22.410 --> 00:24:25.710
A wonderful world, full of dreams and hope.

00:24:26.100 --> 00:24:28.560
The new series 'The Adventures of Tom Sawyer'

00:24:28.560 --> 00:24:30.050
will start this spring!

00:24:30.050 --> 00:24:31.300
Please look forward to it!
